     "type": "application",
     "title": "Score Yourself: Part 1 of 6",
     "content": "Twenty questions done. Count your correct answers and write the number down — you will need all six part scores in Lesson 28.\n\n**The bands.**\n• **18–20 (90–100%)** — mastery. This foundation will carry you through the other five parts.\n• **15–17 (75–85%)** — solid pass. Fix the specific misses; the structure is sound.\n• **14 (70%)** — bare pass. You cleared the line, and you cleared it by one. Treat every miss as required reading.\n• **11–13 (55–65%)** — below the line for this part. Re-read the lessons flagged below before you sit Part 2.\n• **10 or fewer** — the foundation needs rebuilding, not touching up. Stop, go back to the review lessons, then re-sit this part cold.\n\n**Map every miss to its lesson.** Your questions were grouped in blocks, so a wrong answer points straight at one lesson.\n\n• **Q1, Q2, Q3** — anatomy, physiology and body systems. Re-read **Lesson 2, Body Systems, Anatomy & Physiology Refresher.**\n• **Q4, Q5, Q6** — medical terminology and pathophysiology. Re-read **Lesson 3, Medical Terminology & Pathophysiology Refresher.**\n• **Q7, Q8, Q9** — care settings, patient status, licensure and accreditation. Re-read **Lesson 4, The U.S. Healthcare Delivery System & Care Settings.**\n• **Q10, Q11** — credentials, credentialing bodies and professional ethics. Re-read **Lesson 5, The HIM Profession: Roles, Credentials, Ethics & Accreditation.**\n• **Q12, Q13, Q14, Q15, Q16** — record content, documentation standards, authentication and analysis. Re-read **Lesson 6, The Health Record: Content, Documentation Standards & Formats.**\n• **Q17, Q18** — data sets, secondary data and the UHDDS definitions. Re-read **Lesson 7, Data Sets, Registries & Secondary Data Sources.**\n• **Q19, Q20** — MPI integrity, retention, legal hold and destruction. Re-read **Lesson 8, Record Management: MPI, Retention, Destruction & Information Governance.**\n\n**How to read your own pattern.** Two misses scattered across two different blocks is noise — you will absorb those from the explanations. **Two or more misses inside one block is a signal**, and that lesson goes on your re-read list before exam day. Five misses concentrated in the Lesson 6 block matters more than five spread evenly, because record content feeds Parts 2, 4 and 6 as well.\n\nWrite your score, note your flagged lessons, and move to **Lesson 23, Final Exam Part 2: Law, Privacy, Security & Disclosure.** Do not go back and repair your answers first. The exam is worth more to you honest than it is worth perfect.",
